Makes each module archive hold only that module's own objects.

skia_component() is a complete static library in a static build
(gn/BUILDCONFIG.gn). Such an archive copies in the objects of every
non-component dependency:
  - skshaper.lib carried all of HarfBuzz (76 objects) beside harfbuzz.lib, and
    skparagraph.lib took them over once skshaper stopped,
  - svg.lib, sksg.lib and skottie.lib each carried the ~300 objects of :core
    and :pathops through their direct dependency on the :pathops source set,
    which skia.lib already holds,
  - svg.lib and skottie.lib carried skresources.
The duplicates link (they are the same objects), but an archive then no longer
says which component it needs, which a consumer that picks features by archive
depends on.

This sets complete_static_lib = false on svg, sksg, skottie, skshaper and
skparagraph and
drops their :pathops dependency. :skia is untouched.

diff --git a/modules/skottie/BUILD.gn b/modules/skottie/BUILD.gn
index fc95703..eee0b09 100644
--- a/modules/skottie/BUILD.gn
+++ b/modules/skottie/BUILD.gn
@@ -16,13 +16,21 @@ if (skia_enable_skottie) {
 
   skia_component("skottie") {
     check_includes = false
+    # skia-prep: archive only this module's own objects. A component is a
+    # complete static library by default (gn/BUILDCONFIG.gn), which copies
+    # every non-component dependency into it (HarfBuzz into skshaper and
+    # skparagraph, skresources into svg and skottie). The package ships
+    # those as archives of their own.
+    complete_static_lib = false
     import("skottie.gni")
     public_configs = [ ":public_config" ]
     public = skia_skottie_public
     sources = skia_skottie_sources
     configs = [ "../../:skia_private" ]
     deps = [
-      "../..:pathops",
+      # skia-prep: pathops is a source set over :core, so depending on it
+      # copied about 300 of skia's objects into this archive. skia.lib /
+      # libskia.a already holds pathops.
       "../..:skia",
       "../jsonreader",
       "../skresources",
